# API Route Conventions

## Auth

Always resolve the current user through `defineApi` (default `auth: true`), which calls `validateAndGetUser(event)`. Never read the session cookie or `event.context` in a route handler.

```ts
// BAD
export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const session = await auth.api.getSession({ headers: event.headers })
})

// GOOD
export default defineApi({
  handler: async ({ user, event }) => {
    await validateWorkspaceAccess(getRouterParam(event, 'workspaceId')!, user.id)
    return { data: { ... }, message: '...' }
  },
})
```

`server/api/auth/[...all].ts` is the only exception — it is Better Auth's catch-all. Public invite preview uses `defineApi({ auth: false, ... })`.

## Imports

- Use the `~/` alias: `~/lib/prisma`, `~/server/utils/http`. Never `@/` in `server/**`.
- Reusable logic belongs in `server/utils/*.ts`. Access checks use `workspaceAccessWhere` via `validateWorkspaceAccess`, `validateProjectAccess`, `validateTaskAccess`, `validateColumnAccess`. Person rows use `personSelect` / `serializePerson` / `serializeMember` from `~/server/utils/person` only — do not re-export those names from other utils (Nuxt auto-import collides).
- Utils that call each other import explicitly — do not rely on Nuxt auto-import between `server/utils` files.

## Handler shape

```ts
export default defineApi({
  body: workspaceCreateSchema, // Zod; omit on GET/DELETE with no body
  handler: async ({ user, event, body }) => {
    // business logic only
    return { data: { workspace }, message: 'Workspace created successfully', status: 201 }
  },
})
```

Do not wrap handlers in try/catch. `defineApi` parses the body/query, runs auth, returns `{ data, message }`, sets 201 when `status: 201`, and rethrows `createError` preserving `statusCode`. Unexpected errors log via `console.error` and become 500.

## Errors

- Always `throw createError({ statusCode, message })`. Never `return new Response(...)` and never the `statusMessage` key.
- Validate request bodies and queries with Zod schemas from `~/server/utils/schemas`. Do not spread `readBody()` into Prisma.

## Responses

- Success responses are always `{ data, message }`. `data` holds the resource(s). Don't duplicate the HTTP status code inside the JSON body.
- Never return a raw Prisma `User`. Use `serializeAppUser` / `serializePerson` / `serializeMember`.
- For handlers that create a resource, return `status: 201`.

## Cleanup

No leftover `console.log` debugging in committed handlers.
